WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.240
The, Pepe has become kind of a symbol

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.110
We live in perilous times when it comes to
free speech,

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.960
and the threats are coming from both the left
and right.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.760
So we're gonna open up those libel laws folks,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.960
and we're gonna have people sue you like you
never got sued before.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.680
The president has threatened legal action
against the media,

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.710
and progressive activists have used violence

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.820
to shut down campus speakers they don't like.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.180
In The Los Angeles Times,

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.100
former federal prosecutor Ken White shreds
the most popular clichés

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.800
used by used by would-be censors

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.520
trying to make the rest of us shut the hell
up.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.360
That's technically true,

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.800
but the Supreme Court has ruled that those
exceptions are extremely limited.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.579
It’s true that the there are carve outs
for libel, defamation,

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:55.420
true threats of immediate violence, and obscenity.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.120
Page 108, paragraph 3,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.620
no jokes dealing with flatulence, excretion,
urination, ejaculation,

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:01.780
or other bodily functions.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.640
Also note paragraph 2, no use of the so-called
seven dirty words.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.440
These are: cocksucker, motherfucker, fuck,
shit, cunt, cock, and pussy.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.439
But the fact is, that opponents of free speech

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.180
have greatly exaggerated the limits to what
we’re allowed to say.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.020
We're irreverent to the point that we're actually
iconoclastic.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.340
And we offend people.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.979
Hate speech, including horrible, ugly, and
stupid statements

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.360
is broadly protected.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.780
As Ken White points out,

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.340
even outright bigotry isn't exception to the
First Amendment.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.920
There might be a philosophical case for this
position,

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.549
but there's no legal one.

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:55.850
The courts don't do cost/benefit analyses
on specific speech acts.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:00.930
And if the speech doesn't fall into a prohibited
category, you can't stop it.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.210
This widely misquoted line by Supreme Court
Justice Oliver Wendel Holmes, Jr.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.840
has often been used as a justification for
censorship.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.040
As Ken White points out, speech is only prohibited
if it’s

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.999
“intended and likely to provoke imminent
lawless action.”

00:02:15.999 --> 00:02:18.939
So if you see someone getting ready to throw
a tomato

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.800
knock the crap out of them, would yeah?

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.820
Seriously.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.660
Fact is that over time the Supreme Court has
only expanded free speech.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.280
Even cases involving videos of animals being
tortured

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.719
or the Westboro Baptist Church’s demonstrations
at military funerals

00:02:39.719 --> 00:02:44.540
have yielded solid 8-to-1 majorities in favor
of free speech.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.510
If today's calls for suppressing speech teach
us anything,

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.580
it's that we can never take the First Amendment
for granted.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.959
Even if the Supreme Court is on our side,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.220
free expression will only continue to exist

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.920
for as long as we’re willing to make it ourselves.

